{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_roadmap_commercial_roadmap", "label": "The commercial roadmap", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Seven numbered items, nine features (item 6 is three); the numbering is load-bearing because four places in the repo cite it. Sizes are planning-time engineering weeks, a floor, 27-41 weeks summed."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_from_file_to_product", "label": "From File to Product (artifact)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The prose original, drafted 17 August 2026, revised 19 August, against v1.12.3; carries the argument for the Marketplace and for the service producing the file rather than replacing it. Lives outside the repository."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_order_by_dependency", "label": "The roadmap is ordered by dependency, not score", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The product refuses a priority score (ADR 0004), so ranking its own roadmap with one would be incoherent; where two items could swap the original says why they do not."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_item_1_oauth_marketplace", "label": "Item 1: OAuth app on the Marketplace", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Done, as both routes: OAuth 2.0 3LO in scripts/jira_auth.py for pulling your own board, and a Forge app at 4.0.0 for the tenant install."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_item_2_organisation_configuration", "label": "Item 2: Organisation configuration", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shipped inverted: assumptions resolved once at the point of production and written into the dataset as orgConfig rather than exposed as a file each consumer opens."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_item_3_scheduled_delivery", "label": "Item 3: Scheduled delivery of the two views", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Delivered 2026-08-26 with no channel and no mail provider: Jira sends the brief as a notification on an anchor issue; the model is Atlassian-hosted @forge/llm so no issue titles leave the boundary. It touches item 5, which was not written down."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_item_4_durable_sprint_history", "label": "Item 4: Durable sprint history (4a/4b/4c)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "4a records figures a re-derivation can disagree with; 4b lifts the six-sprint window into trendSprints; 4c is the forecast log, logging capacity claims (p% of at least N items by D) that hold no issue keys. A log needs ten resolved forecasts before it scores."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_item_5_permission_mirroring", "label": "Item 5: Permission mirroring", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "First pass only: three exposures (series store, forecast log, brief) answered by accepting and naming a disclosure; no permission model built, so none of the 5-8 week estimate has been spent against what was estimated. Flagged as under-estimated; plan against the upper bound."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_item_6_sso_audit_residency", "label": "Item 6: SSO, audit log, data residency", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Residency arrived early as a side effect of the Cloud Run calculator, region-pinned per installation by Forge; the audit log is an operational activity log that is not tamper-evident and says so; SSO needed nothing because the app owns no identity."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_item_7_rollup_and_sequencing", "label": "Item 7: Cross-team roll-up and intake sequencing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Roll-up names the boards it covers and refuses to forecast. Sequencing refused on Forge until 2026-08-31 not for items 4 or 5 but because nobody had decided what an ask is inside Jira; the answer was a declared Candidate field and a T-Shirt Size band, not an issue type."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_activity_log", "label": "Activity log, not audit log", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Jira's audit API is read-only and reading it needs Administer Jira, so the app writes its own operational log and says it is not tamper-evident; a record the app could not have falsified needs a customer-controlled sink and is unsized."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_forecast_log", "label": "The forecast log (4c)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A published forecast writes capacity claims to the board's log (app storage on Forge, git-ignored file over loopback); a what-if writes nothing; claims resolve when their horizon passes and the tile prints the scorer's own sentence including its refusal."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_three_standing_refusals", "label": "The three standing refusals", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never rank individuals (ADR 0003), never compute a priority score (ADR 0004), no hours or timesheets. Sold as the reason the numbers can be trusted rather than as missing features; the lost deals would have churned when the data failed the claim."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_hostnames_and_realms_decision", "label": "Hostnames and realms settled once", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "*.run.app permanently, and three realms US, EU, GB (London service, because the UK is its own realm and the first customer is a UK company). Both answered 2026-08-31 while the only install was development; changing later is a major version and a reinstall for every customer."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_single_file_versus_hosted_service", "label": "The single-file promise fights the hosted service", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Has happened twice: the Monte Carlo tile (ADR 0008) and item 3. The security suite stays the arbiter (no network, no storage in the produced file) and every future feature answers the fork out loud; a tile degrading to an honest notice is acceptable, three of them is a dashboard URL with extra steps."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_assets_unclaimed", "label": "Assets held but unclaimed", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A forecaster that refuses below a data threshold, and WCAG 2.2 AA already tested in both themes: a VPAT is a fortnight of documentation that unlocks public-sector procurement."}, {"id": "agent_tools_forecast_score_calibration", "label": "forecast.score_calibration()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agent_tools_intake_asks_from_issues", "label": "intake.asks_from_issues()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "scripts_jira_auth", "label": "scripts/jira_auth.py", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "forge_src_series", "label": "forge/src/series.js", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_roadmap_commercial_roadmap", "target": "docs_roadmap_from_file_to_product", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_roadmap_commercial_roadmap", "target": "docs_roadmap_order_by_dependency", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_roadmap_commercial_roadmap", "target": "docs_roadmap_item_1_oauth_marketplace", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_roadmap_commercial_roadmap", "target": "docs_roadmap_item_2_organisation_configuration", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/roadmap.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"s